  "name": "COVID 19 NEUTRALIZING ANTIBODY IgG - I",
  "code": "2003",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"64\" data-end=\"318\">The <strong data-start=\"68\" data-end=\"111\">COVID-19 Neutralizing Antibody IgG Test</strong> measures levels of <strong data-start=\"131\" data-end=\"209\">IgG antibodies that block the SARS-CoV-2 virus from binding to human cells</strong>, specifically by inhibiting the interaction between the virus's <strong data-start=\"274\" data-end=\"291\">spike protein</strong> and the <strong data-start=\"300\" data-end=\"317\">ACE2 receptor</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"320\" data-end=\"456\">These antibodies are functionally important because they can <strong data-start=\"381\" data-end=\"429\">prevent infection or reduce disease severity</strong> by neutralizing the virus.</p>\n<p data-start=\"463\" data-end=\"490\"><strong data-start=\"467\" data-end=\"490\">Purpose of the Test</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"492\" data-end=\"748\">\n<li data-start=\"492\" data-end=\"558\">\n<p data-start=\"494\" data-end=\"558\">To evaluate <strong data-start=\"506\" data-end=\"518\">immunity</strong> after natural infection or vaccination.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"559\" data-end=\"626\">\n<p data-start=\"561\" data-end=\"626\">To assess the <strong data-start=\"575\" data-end=\"600\">neutralizing capacity</strong> of the antibody response.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"627\" data-end=\"748\">\n<p data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"748\">Sometimes used before or after <strong data-start=\"660\" data-end=\"691\">monoclonal antibody therapy</strong>, or to assess response in immunocompromised individuals.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive / Reactive</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates the presence of <strong>neutralizing IgG antibodies</strong>. Suggests prior infection or vaccination has triggered an immune response capable of inhibiting the virus.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative / Non-reactive</strong></td>\n<td>No detectable neutralizing IgG antibodies. Could mean the person is unexposed, recently infected without antibody development yet, or a <strong>poor immune response</strong> (e.g., immunocompromised).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Borderline / Equivocal</strong></td>\n<td>Inconclusive result; may require repeat testing or correlation with total antibody levels and clinical history.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
